[align=center]
[img]https://switch-vision.zemerdon.com/icon_pack/installation.png[/img]
[size=200][b]Start Here — Install & Update Switch Vision[/b][/size]
[color=#5B8DEF][i]The recommended path from Home Assistant to a working Switch Vision dashboard[/i][/color]
[/align]
[hr]
[notice][b]You only need one repository.[/b]
https://github.com/zemerdon/switch-vision-installer
Switch Vision Installer manages the remaining Switch Vision components.[/notice]

[size=150][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Home Assistant OS or Supervised with App/Supervisor support
[*]Access to Home Assistant /config and /share
[*]MQTT available to Home Assistant
[*]For SNMP switches: read-only SNMP v2c access
[*]For UniFi API devices: a supported local UniFi controller and read-only Integration API credentials
[/list]

[size=150][b]Fresh installation[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Add the Switch Vision Installer repository.
[*]Install and open [b]Switch Vision Installer[/b].
[*]Install the recommended Switch Vision components.
[*]Restart Home Assistant Core when requested.
[*]Open [b]Settings → Devices & services[/b].
[*]Add or confirm the [b]Switch Vision[/b] integration.
[*]Open [b]Switch Vision Hub[/b]. The Home Assistant app itself is named [b]Switch Vision Discovery[/b].
[*]Add your switch or switches.
[*]Normally leave [b]Switch Model[/b] on [b]Auto-detect[/b].
[*]Run [b]Discovery[/b].
[*]Open [b]Switch Vision[/b] from the Home Assistant sidebar.
[/list]

[size=150][b]Updating[/b][/size]
[code]Switch Vision Installer
→ Update All
→ restart Home Assistant Core when requested
→ hard-refresh the browser if old frontend content remains[/code]
[b]Update All[/b] is dependency-aware and is the preferred upgrade workflow.
Do not manually mix Core, Discovery or other files from different release generations.

[size=150][b]Component versions[/b][/size]
Switch Vision components have independent version lines. That is normal.
The Installer shows installed and currently available versions and is the normal user-facing version authority.
Current Core: [b]v2.6.8[/b]. Protected Gold baseline: [b]v2.5.0 Gold[/b].

[size=150][b]Discovery configuration[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Switch Name (Used internally only)[/b] — stable unique internal ID
[*][b]Display name[/b] — friendly dashboard name
[*][b]Management IP / hostname[/b]
[*][b]Sensor prefix[/b]
[*][b]SNMP community[/b] — read-only
[*][b]Walk mode[/b] — Targeted is normally recommended
[*][b]Switch Model[/b] — normally Auto-detect
[/list]
For a stack, configure the parent switch and add each member with its own member number, display name and sensor prefix.

[size=150][b]What Discovery does[/b][/size]
[code]Validate switches
→ collect current switch data
→ identify exact model and interfaces
→ match the device registry
→ generate telemetry configuration
→ generate dashboard cards
→ validate the handoff
→ start/restart SNMP2MQTT when required
→ update Switch Vision[/code]

[notice]Discovery uses current-run SNMP evidence by default. Old walk files are not silently treated as current switch data.[/notice]

[size=150][b]Existing installations[/b][/size]
Use the Installer's update path and follow any restart instructions it gives you.
